<!-- Armor Page -->
<div data-role="page" class="jqm-demos jqm-home" id="armor">

<%= erb :'sections/header' %>
<%= erb :'sections/nav-panel' %>
<%= erb :'sections/search-panel', locals: {loaded: @loaded} %>
<% @loaded = 'true' %>

    <div role="main" class="ui-content">
            <div class="jqm-block-content">
                <h3>Magic Armor</h3>
                <p>Magic Armor is provided by some Enchantments. The specific enchantment will denote a number of points of Magic Armor that are granted to each hit location</p>
                <ol>
                    <li>If Magic Armor is granted from two different sources, only the highest value present is used and all others are ignored. Example: A player is wearing Barkskin (1 point of Magic Armor) and receives Stoneskin (2 points of Magic Armor). Since Stoneskin is higher value, their current and maximum armor values increase by 1. If the player removes Stoneskin while keeping Barkskin, their current and maximum armor values are reduced by 1
                    <ol type="a">
                        <li>Until all sources of Magic Armor are completely removed, Magic Armor tracks damage by hit location. Example: A player wearing Stoneskin takes a point of damage. They now have 1 point of Magic Armor in that location out of a maximum value of 2. They gain Barkskin, and then remove Stoneskin. That hit location now has 0 points of Magic Armor out of a maximum value of 1</li>
                    </ol>
                    </li>
                    <li>Magic Armor may be the target of abilities that affect armor such as Armor Breaking, Fireball, etc.</li>
                    <li>Magic Armor may be repaired like any other armor</li>
                    <li>Magic Armor covers all locations on a player without any gaps in coverage</li>
                    <li>Unless it is inherently part of the Enchantment, Magic Armor can never benefit from armor enhancement abilities such as Ancestral Armor or Harden Armor</li>
                    <li>Players may wear more Magic Armor than their class maximum allows. A class which cannot wear any armor can still wear Magic Armor</li>
                    <li>Magic Armor behaves identically to normal armor</li>
                    <li>Enchantments which grant Magic Armor fail when targeting a player with worn armor. Players may not don worn armor while bearing an enchantment which grants magic armor. (If you are only wearing armor that was rated initially as zero points it may be worn with Magic Armor.)</li>
                </ol>
                <p><i><a href="#magic-definitions">All Magic Definitions</a></i></p>
            </div>

    </div><!-- /footer -->

    </div><!-- /content -->

</div>
<!-- Armor /page -->

<!-- Magic Balls Page -->
<div data-role="page" class="jqm-demos jqm-home" id="magicballs">

<%= erb :'sections/header' %>
<%= erb :'sections/nav-panel' %>
<%= erb :'sections/search-panel', locals: {loaded: @loaded} %>
<% @loaded = 'true' %>

    <div role="main" class="ui-content">
            <div class="jqm-block-content">
                <h3>Magic Balls</h3>
                <p>Magic Balls which are thrown and strike a player or object can have various effects (see list of <a href="/spells/balls" data-ajax="false">Magic Balls</a>)</p>
                <ol>
                    <li>Players may only carry or bring on to the battlefield a number of Magic Balls up to the maximum uses allowed to them
                        <ol type="a">
                            <li>Owners of Magic Balls may grant other players permission to carry their Magic Balls in order to return them to the owner or to the owner's base. They may also grant other players permission to use their Magic Balls if the other player has the ability to do so</li>
                        </ol>
                    </li>
                    <li>A Magic Ball must be held in the caster's hand by the end of the incantation to become active</li>
                    <li>A Magic Ball will become inactive if the caster begins an incantation or the Magic Ball stops being held in hand and has not been thrown. The caster can transfer an active Magic Ball from one hand to the other without it becoming inactive and can wield a weapon or shield in a hand that is also holding an active Magic Ball</li>
                    <li>A player may only have one Magic Ball active at a time</li>
                    <li>Magic balls affect the first valid player or equipment struck, then become inactive.  A Magic Ball that strikes terrain becomes inactive with no effect.  Garb strikes count as hitting whatever target a Magic Ball would have continued on to hit, had it not struck garb.  For example, you may not block Lightning Bolts with your cloak
                        <ol type="a">
                            <li>A Magic Ball that strikes armor will damage the armor if armor points remain and the ball is Armor Breaking or Armor Destroying.</li>
                            <li>A Weapon Destroying or Shield Destroying Magic Ball that strikes equipment will affect that equipment</li>
                            <li>A Magic Ball that strikes unwielded equipment will affect both that equipment and whatever the Magic Ball would have struck if the unwielded equipment were not there</li>
                        </ol>
                    <li>Engulfing Magic Balls affect a player upon striking a valid hit location, carried equipment, or garb, and then become inactive</li>
                    <li>Magic Balls are not stopped by Protection from Projectiles, Song of Deflection, or similar abilities</li>
                </ol>
                <p><i><a href="#magic-definitions">All Magic Definitions</a></i></p>
            </div>

    </div><!-- /footer -->

    </div><!-- /content -->

</div>
<!-- Magic Balls /page -->

<!-- Meta-magic Page -->
<div data-role="page" class="jqm-demos jqm-home" id="metamagic">

<%= erb :'sections/header' %>
